      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Spinal epidural lipomatosis (SEL) is a condition in which excess adipose tissue is deposited circumferentially about the spinal cord in the epidural space. It is most frequently seen in patients on chronic glucocorticosteroid therapy for a variety of medical problems. This is a case report of lumbar epidural lipomatosis in a bodybuilder with radiculopathy supposedly induced by anabolic steroid intake."},
